  "description": "Random cell iterator. Table mode (weather 6.7, G2): every reset refills the table with the rectangle's ABSOLUTE packed coordinates (x mod 256) << 8 | (z mod 256) in natural order (x outer, z inner) - the dirty flag is never cleared - then random_shuffles it when asked (n - 1 rand() calls, none without shuffling); next() walks the table and returns the absolute coordinates; the reset leaves the prime-step current and step unchanged. Expected tables from an independent Python model of foundations 12.1 (rand from state 1) and 12.3 (random_shuffle): reset 1 [769, 1, 768, ...], reset 2 refills before shuffling again (so it is a shuffle of the natural order, not of reset 1's table), reset 3 without shuffle gives natural order; weather test 11 ([2, 3] x [5, 6] -> 0x0205, 0x0206, 0x0305, 0x0306, then false; current/step kept); coordinates above 255 wrap [quirk]. Prime-step mode: one rand() call per shuffling reset. A never-reset (constructed) iterator has count 0 and its first next() returns false.",
